From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: veldenb <062a2dfa2234@sinenomine.email>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 17:13:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia: treat an unmap of an unregistered DMA mapping range
 as a no-op

virtmemUnmapFrom() asserted and returned NV_ERR_INVALID_OBJECT_HANDLE when
intermapGetDmaMapping() found nothing for the requested offset.

That situation is reachable: the VA space splits mappings at mapping page
boundaries while the resource server tracks inter-mappings as byte ranges,
so an earlier partial unmap can already have released the pages a
server-side fragment still describes.  It also happens when inter-mapping
registration fails after the client mapping was torn down.

Failing the unmap leaves the server-side inter-mapping node in place, and
a later mapping at the same dmaOffset then fails with

  NVRM: refAddInterMapping: Duplicate inter mapping detected ...
  NVRM: Check failed: 0 == (pMapNode->gpuMask & gpuMask) @ gpu_vaspace.c

Log the request and return NV_OK instead, so that cleanup paths (notably
the automatic unmapping of back references in rs_client.c) can retire
their bookkeeping.

Related: #1364, #1453, #1483.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit adae9fd31c4e153db8ad560e43f41538ffa68267)
---
 src/nvidia/src/kernel/mem_mgr/virtual_mem.c | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/nvidia/src/kernel/mem_mgr/virtual_mem.c b/src/nvidia/src/kernel/mem_mgr/virtual_mem.c
index 76026674..29947f92 100644
--- a/src/nvidia/src/kernel/mem_mgr/virtual_mem.c
+++ b/src/nvidia/src/kernel/mem_mgr/virtual_mem.c
@@ -1583,7 +1583,27 @@ virtmemUnmapFrom_IMPL
 
     // Get DMA mapping info.
     pDmaMappingInfo = intermapGetDmaMapping(pVirtualMemory, dmaOffset);
-    NV_ASSERT_OR_RETURN(pDmaMappingInfo != NULL, NV_ERR_INVALID_OBJECT_HANDLE);
+    if (pDmaMappingInfo == NULL)
+    {
+        //
+        // Nothing is registered for this range any more.
+        //
+        // This happens when an earlier partial unmap already released the
+        // pages containing the request (the VA space splits at mapping page
+        // boundaries while the resource server tracks byte ranges), or when
+        // inter-mapping registration failed after the client mapping had
+        // been torn down.  Treat the unmap as a no-op so that cleanup paths
+        // (notably the automatic unmapping of back references in
+        // rs_client.c) can retire their own bookkeeping instead of failing
+        // and leaving stale inter-mapping nodes behind, which later surface
+        // as "Duplicate inter mapping" / "0 == (pMapNode->gpuMask & gpuMask)"
+        // failures on unrelated mappings.
+        //
+        NV_PRINTF(LEVEL_ERROR,
+                  "Unmap of unregistered DMA mapping range [0x%llX, 0x%llX); ignoring.\n",
+                  dmaOffset, dmaOffset + pParams->size);
+        return NV_OK;
+    }
     NvBool bPartialUnmap = dmaOffset != pDmaMappingInfo->DmaOffset || pParams->size != pDmaMappingInfo->pMemDesc->Size;
     NV_ASSERT_OR_RETURN(!bPartialUnmap || !bIsIndirectPeer, NV_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT);
 
